PART 2: RIEMANN ZETA AT NEGATIVE INTEGERS
======================================================================

ζ(s) at negative odd integers:
  ζ(- 1) = -B_2/2 =           -1/12 = -0.083333
  ζ(- 3) = -B_4/4 =           1/120 = 0.008333
  ζ(- 5) = -B_6/6 =          -1/252 = -0.003968
  ζ(- 7) = -B_8/8 =           1/240 = 0.004167
  ζ(- 9) = -B_10/10 =          -1/132 = -0.007576
  ζ(-11) = -B_12/12 =       691/32760 = 0.021093
  ζ(-13) = -B_14/14 =           -1/12 = -0.083333
  ζ(-15) = -B_16/16 =       3617/8160 = 0.443260
  ζ(-17) = -B_18/18 =    -43867/14364 = -3.053954
  ζ(-19) = -B_20/20 =     174611/6600 = 26.456212

ζ(s) at negative even integers (trivial zeros):
  ζ(-2) = 0
  ζ(-4) = 0
  ζ(-6) = 0
  ζ(-8) = 0
  ζ(-10) = 0

--- Comparison with forbidden H values ---
ζ(-1) = -B_2/2 = -1/12 = -0.0833
ζ(-3) = -B_4/4 = 1/120 = 0.008333
ζ(-5) = -B_6/6 = -1/252 = -0.003968
ζ(-7) = -B_8/8 = 1/240 = 0.004167

Forbidden H values: 7, 21
ζ(-3) = 1/120 ≠ 7
ζ(-5) = -1/252 ≠ 21
So the STANDARD Riemann zeta does NOT directly give 7 and 21.

